EXT. SALOON ROOF - HIGH NOON

Heat. Dust. A rain barrel on a flat tin roof.

SHERIFF AMOS TEAGUE crouches behind a chimney, rifle ready. EZEKIEL, teenager, deputy, hugs the roofline. TWO-FINGER MAGGIE, fifties, a bartender, pulls a shotgun from her apron. CHEN WEI, thirties, a railway cook, grips a cleaver. RAFAEL, forties, a horse trader, holds a pistol. HOLLIS, sixty, the town drunk, flops on his back, a bottle on his chest.

Hooves below. A gang enters Main Street.

TEAGUE
Hold fire.

EZEKIEL
They're coming.

TEAGUE
I said hold.

MAGGIE
They'll see us, Amos!

CHEN WEI
They won't look up.

RAFAEL ^
They always look up!

Guns crack. Dust jumps. Hollis lifts the bottle, toasts the sky, and drinks.
